  "title": "Erdős Problem #809",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 3$ and define $F_k(n)$ to be the minimal $r$ such that there is a graph $G$ on $n$ vertices with $\\lfloor n^2/4\\rfloor+1$ many edges such that the edges can be $r$-coloured so that every subgraph isomorphic to $C_{2k+1}$ has no colour repeating on the edges.\nIs it true that $ F_k(n)\\sim n^2/8? $ ",
